R-SO14 R-SO15 R-SO23 R-FE4 R-LF1 R-DL1 R-DL5 R-NI5 R-EF1 R-CM3 R-CM9 R-PTH2 (slice 072c): the fetch flows that slice 072b did not wire, with no compiler at all (no `roc` on PATH, nothing installed, no `default-roc`) and a package that is not in the cache. 5 runs, each in its own home (`h1` to `h5`, no compiler). `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=yes` (in `fx/env`) is the consent.
The project p1 is a package file with one entry, `json` (acme/json 2.2.0, hash HJ). Each home has `compat.tsv` with the facts for HJ: pass on N1 (10-14) and N2 (10-16), fail on N3 (10-18). The channel (the list route) has N1 to N4 (10-19, the latest). So R-SO14 (1) (c) picks N2, the newest compiler that passes for HJ, and not the latest, N4: the proof that the flow passes the hashes of its project (R-SO23: the project of the command).
Run 1 (`list`), run 2 (`why json`), run 3 (`path json`), run 4 (`patch json`): the fetch of the closure needs `roc unbundle`, so the flow downloads N2 (the prompt text is the answer line on stderr, `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=yes` has no prompt), sets it as `default-roc` (R-SO15, no default was set: `config.toml` is made), and unbundles the package with it. Then the command goes on as before (the list, the paths, the patch copy). The exit code was 18 (`no compiler is selected`) for each of them before slice 072c: these flows passed `Stop`. The request of `tln list`, `why`, `outdated` and `patch` (`Ls.request_of`) had the consent `Ask` and ignored `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL`: it has the consent facts of the environment now.
Run 5 (`outdated`): the command reads the index of acme/json (2.3.0 is newer) and the facts, and fetches no package, so it needs no compiler and downloads none (R-LF1). It shows that the wiring of `OutdatedFlow` is not reached by this fixture: no test reaches `Walk` for it.
Not here: `verify`, `remove`, `roc use`, `probe` (see the slice file, question Q2 and the gap table): with no pin they stop at `check_pin` before any fetch (slice 072d), and with a pin that is not installed the choice of the compiler for `roc unbundle` is question Q2. `init` is the case `init/it4-nocompiler`. `run` has no fetch of its own.
